Third-party components with separate licensing terms
---------------------------------------------------------------------

The following component ships alongside SAPMAP but is licensed
separately from SAPMAP's own Apache-2.0 grant.  These components
are invoked via subprocess boundaries (fork/exec), not linked into
SAPMAP's own Python address space, so SAPMAP itself remains
Apache-2.0.

  * tools/sap_decompress/sap_decompress
      Precompiled ELF binary that decompresses SAP's proprietary
      LZH format (used inside GET_TABLEBLOCK_COMPRESSED_RFC
      responses).  Built from the pysap project's pysapcompress
      module — see https://github.com/OpenCyberTranslated/pysap.
      pysap is distributed under the GNU General Public License
      version 2 (GPL-2.0).  SAPMAP invokes this binary via
      subprocess only; it does not link the pysap library into
      its own process.

      Full GPL-2.0 text: https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/gpl-2.0.txt

      A tools/sap_decompress/README.md file in this repository
      describes the binary's provenance and how to rebuild it
      from pysap sources for architectures other than x86-64
      Linux.

